Create one illustration of a Patchouli Knowledge (Touhou Project) fumo-style stuffed plush doll, seated on a simple wooden tabletop. Oversized broad round head, tiny stuffed body, short arms and two stubby legs forward. Deadpan half-lidded embroidered eyes and tiny stitched mouth, fabric bangs and long side locks, frilled crescent-moon cap, bows at cap sides and side locks, ruffled striped dress. Keep unmistakable plush-toy proportions and cloth construction, not a human character. Full doll entirely inside a square frame with breathing room, nearly frontal view. Soft light from the left; simple quiet background. No words, signature, watermark, other dolls, people or extra props. Medium: finished black-and-white manga ink drawing on white paper. Confident tapered pen strokes and varied line weight, heavier outer silhouette and delicate interior stitching and folds. Model the stuffed volume with sparse directional cross-hatching and a few controlled black shadow shapes. White paper remains dominant; light screentone only in selected shadows. Draw fibers with a few intentional marks, not photorealistic texture. Express the purple costume through distinct ink values rather than color. Face and crescent clearly readable. Background suggested with a few economical lines. No color, soft airbrush shading or photographic rendering.